sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as 👤 Viewer / Judge
    participant UI as 🖥️ Next.js Web (frontend)
    participant API as ⚙️ Express API (backend)
    participant Redis as ⚡ Redis Hot Cache
    participant DB as 🗄️ Supabase (PostgreSQL)
    participant Disk as 📂 /data/cache/*.json
    participant SerpApi as 🔍 SerpApi Engines
    participant FactCheck as ✅ Google Fact Check API
    participant LLM as 🧠 LLM Provider

    User->>UI: Submits YouTube Video URL
    UI->>API: POST /api/videos/process { youtubeUrl }

    Note over API,Redis: Check if video was already processed
    API->>Redis: GET video:{youtubeVideoId}
    alt Video Cache Hit (Hot Cache)
        Redis-->>API: Return cached video analysis
    else Video Cache Miss
        API->>DB: Query videos table by youtubeVideoId
        alt DB Hit
            DB-->>API: Return stored claims & verdicts
        else DB Miss
            Note over API,SerpApi: Stage 1: Transcript Fetching
            API->>SerpApi: youtube_video_transcript (1 credit)
            SerpApi-->>API: Raw transcript segments with timestamps
            API->>Disk: Write /data/cache/{videoId}_transcript.json

            Note over API,LLM: Stage 2 & 3: Extraction & Classification
            API->>LLM: Extract checkable claims (Health / Financial / General)
            LLM-->>API: List of typed claims with timestamp_seconds

            loop For Each Extracted Claim
                Note over API,Redis: Deduplication Check (Normalized Claim Hash)
                API->>Redis: GET claim:{claimHash}
                alt Claim Cache Hit
                    Redis-->>API: Return cached verdict & evidence
                else Claim Cache Miss
                    Note over API,FactCheck: Stage 4: Fact Check Lookup
                    API->>FactCheck: claims:search?query={claimText}
                    alt Fact Check Found
                        FactCheck-->>API: claimReview result with textualRating
                        API->>Disk: Write /data/cache/{claimId}_fact_check.json
                    else No Fact Check Match
                        Note over API,SerpApi: Stage 5: SerpApi Grounding Fallback
                        alt Health Claim
                            API->>SerpApi: google_scholar (query core claim)
                        else Financial Claim
                            API->>SerpApi: google_finance (ticker / entity)
                        else General Claim
                            API->>SerpApi: google (natural language query)
                        end
                        SerpApi-->>API: Organic results / financial snapshot
                        API->>Disk: Write /data/cache/{claimId}_{sourceType}.json
                    end

                    Note over API,LLM: Stage 6: Scoring Algorithm
                    API->>LLM: Evaluate Grounding Similarity (0.0 to 1.0)
                    LLM-->>API: Grounding score
                    API->>API: Compute Source Authority Score & Trust Score (Grounding × Authority)
                    API->>API: Assign Confidence Label (High Confidence / Contested / Unverified)

                    Note over API,DB: Write-Through Persistence
                    API->>DB: Insert claim, evidence, and verdict records
                    API->>Redis: SET claim:{claimHash} (cached verdict)
                end
            end

            API->>DB: Update video record as processed
            API->>Redis: SET video:{youtubeVideoId}
        end
    end

    API-->>UI: Return timestamped claim ledger + video summary
    UI-->>User: Render interactive claim ledger synchronized with video player
